<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In March, Tottenham, fearing possible rele=
gation, spent big to bring in Roberto De Zerbi, who will probably never go =
into a negotiation with a stronger hand. There was obvious improvement and =
they stayed up on the final day of the season. Since then, Spurs have spent=
 a net =C2=A3175m ($234m) on improving the squad. The message seemed clear:=
 the fiscal caution of the Daniel Levy era was over and this was a club wil=
ling to spend. Yet Spurs go into the first international break <a href=3D"h=
ttps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNt=
ZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEA15UWWoWHBtz4xzueDIlilJPKO0xvMhNrfAUCht_4RlyqcGUGuyquOT_6Z=
4tY3eIJbrCayy81_evJRd7fe5zqnkDx_gkdAdl4u8J1N3GZqQuHILt2qjWG98TUC6UKyfS8ItxO=
G8Tcje3OBIZCShAxMV7vhQfWPrnsQGk3Ig6bq_8wepJZ5-7pVFyK5c7sNyXDXUrM_xoMMMRimbB=
UbJmJXDv-qc_ekbfxdXyDQXqN0SZ_CvlqUWlIK7eEaMid5JiQ/4u8/PJHwantDSkSycGta_GGmR=
w/h5/h001.fx3ld1xDL9TgVJ-cAeFye6F95-qHiMxA10zSRUIIfRQ" style=3D"color: #007=
7B6;">bottom of the Premier League table</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">To an extent, the issue is confidence. On =
the opening weekend at Brentford, with a weird mishmash of a side, a team t=
hat was clearly undercooked, they were hammered 3-0 by much better-prepared=
 opponents. That was not hugely surprising given how sensible Brentford=E2=
=80=99s transfer dealing had been and how early they had done it. More worr=
ying was what happened the following week as Spurs, starting well before fa=
ding, lost 2-0 at home to Newcastle.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Goalless draws against Nottingham Forest a=
nd Everton seemed to have steadied the ship. Their biggest problem seemed t=
o be a lack of confidence. They were tentative in possession, indecisive wh=
en chances did come. The two goals they managed in their <a href=3D"https:/=
/ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIE=
MgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPglhMZqQFchn47HdQmXZKaY-D3jQMxa-BY4kKj6PnL2k=
KY4uH0StjKS5Fg33-zQbWg76YC1wHRtBvER9QY8lkt-Rn8U5jDRDU8b1U70nqTjdQ90WTcYqM6x=
fsMu6xp73UG8BNl92JlufunR35qhXKre3wO6fmwWPQltKfbxdKXJIwcpl4h-DrUWezJlIwhFqYG=
JKMQ2aFZtEQDvfxZxQVEytxW-OqG3ZPfIQe-VDba_IUjNEXxS8-QCib3GgNb6KscR6rpJVHNdea=
ZeEaEJQ3o6Q/4u8/PJHwantDSkSycGta_GGmRw/h6/h001.ZLTtO5qxPUBRZNSiEAeBqjJOx6vP=
Y64vnjiSJXgPN2A" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">3-2 defeat to Aston Villa</a> on=
 Saturday mean Spurs climbed above Coventry to second-bottom of the goal-sc=
oring charts, but they are ninth for shots. That should be reason for frust=
ration rather than panic; the goals will come eventually.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But there are more concerning things to ha=
ve come out of Saturday=E2=80=99s game. The lack of confidence in front of =
goal seems to have curdled into something worse, a more general mental dege=
neration. Again, they started well. The Villa keeper Zion Suzuki made a str=
ing of saves. And then just before half-time Villa scored a shambolic goal.=
 Micky van de Ven was off the pitch receiving treatment. Andy Robertson, in=
 preventing the ball running out for a corner, gifted possession to John Mc=
Ginn. A cut-back, a scuffed shot and Johan Manzambi was unmarked in the six=
-yard box to score. It was a horrible goal to concede.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The second goal they conceded was just as =
bad. A long punt not dealt with, Nicolas Jackson bringing the ball down, Va=
n de Ven not getting tight enough, a shot that bounced in off Antonin Kinsk=
y=E2=80=99s hand. The third Villa goal was whipped brilliantly into the top=
 corner by Emi Buend=C3=ADa, but he had space to line it up before James Ma=
ddison, who had been marking Jo=C3=A3o Gomes, got out to him. Perhaps Maddi=
son could have been more aggressive, and the slight turn of his back as Bue=
nd=C3=ADa struck his shot is never a good sign, but this was at least as mu=
ch a failure of structure.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">To an extent Spurs were unfortunate. Rober=
tson might have cleared that ball for a throw-in, or at least got distance =
down the line, and Boubacar Kamara=E2=80=99s mishit cross could have gone a=
nywhere. Jackson will not always be so deft in taking down a chest-high bal=
l. Buend=C3=ADa, enormously technically gifted as he is, will not always pi=
ck out the top corner. But equally, each goal followed some sort of error: =
the Premier League is full of high-class players who will take advantage of=
 any slip.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">De Zerbi spoke of Spurs being =E2=80=9Ctoo=
 fragile=E2=80=9D, by which he seemed to be talking both of their physicali=
ty and mentality. They have players returning from injury. Like so many clu=
bs, they brought in players late. Preseasons have been curtailed, perhaps i=
nadequate.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Where the initial instinct was to be impre=
ssed by the numbers and the change of policy, doubts are now emerging about=
 the nature of those summer signings. Is Sandro Tonali really worth =C2=A31=
00m? Mateus Fernandes played for a relegated side. Jan Paul van Hecke would=
n=E2=80=99t be the first player to leave Brighton and find his level dip ou=
tside that precisely configured environment. S=C3=A1vio and Omar Marmoush s=
truggled to get into the team at Manchester City. S=C3=A1vio=E2=80=99s fini=
shing brought just two league goals in two seasons at City and the evidence=
 of Saturday is that it has not improved.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The sense had been that this season couldn=
=E2=80=99t be as bad as the last two for Spurs. There is no Europe to distr=
act them. The injury crises couldn=E2=80=99t be as bad again. De Zerbi has =
proved his worth in the Premier League before. They have spent money. And y=
et this is as bad as it=E2=80=99s ever been. Once a club of Tottenham=E2=80=
=99s stature could have dismissed this as a blip, the kind of thing that wo=
uld inevitably sort itself out as the season went on. After the last two se=
asons, nobody can be quite that confident again.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s still implausible Spurs could=
 be relegated, unlikely even that they=E2=80=99ll be in another fight, but =
those preseason thoughts of European qualification are already beginning to=
 look bafflingly optimistic =E2=80=93 and that will inevitably slow the reb=
uilding of the club.</p>
