ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;"><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As English football emerged=
 from the second world war, its claims to be the best in the world were pro=
bably misguided but not entirely spurious. In 1948, England beat the reigni=
ng world champions Italy 4-0 in Turin, the forward line of Stanley Matthews=
, Stan Mortensen, Tommy Lawton, Wilf Mannion and Tom Finney producing what =
was arguably the greatest away result in the team=E2=80=99s history. Althou=
gh their unbeaten record against non-British opposition had ended against S=
pain in Madrid in 1929, they remained undefeated at home. And then, on 21 S=
eptember 1949, England faced the Republic of Ireland at Goodison Park. Asto=
n Villa=E2=80=99s Con Martin put Ireland ahead from the penalty spot. The M=
anchester United right-back Johnny Carey had a superb game stifling Finney.=
 Everton=E2=80=99s Peter Farrell broke through to add a late second and Eng=
land=E2=80=99s home record was gone. Ireland, though, were familiar; three =
of their players had played for Northern Ireland, and most played in the En=
glish system. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001=
.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBYsb93GJSEF_C1-UhtUYc3YFT0UBtYAp=
Jv_WU-rOOEr6NTjYeUBlS2ZJ9Ku12f-leoYz007hnJI762Ha1Vp3g2M_40F4M7KwWjM-1nFzVTB=
O29LMJWW5pQwMluoiYKkLd8KgOnewZkaAANNVtsl9ir9pX1PXNRLKZizJ8AkHfCaWSY84x_GpWo=
-xPEejjmvnmuKh-BuxJprIH4Vv3x95wcEaD7kvNzk-SlAo0PPQQ6zSjWhJm5RGek6TP8lhjf_tM=
UCHiqULqJl7Jbje5RMRtJ/4u8/PJHwantDSkSycGta_GGmRw/h8/h001.FGQPBSUHfgyI9kIrmm=
Vlt0rUUqouNu_zWPHfD03rSYQ" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">The 6-3 defeat at Wemb=
ley to Hungary</a> in November 1953 was felt far more keenly and is widely =
regarded as the moment of English football=E2=80=99s fall, the disgrace tha=
t prompted the soul-searching that brought, 13 years later, the World Cup w=
in. But the home record had been lost against Ireland at Goodison.</p></div=
